 "intro": "Near Nisibis in Mesopotamia, 217 AD. The Emperor Caracalla has been murdered. You are Macrinus, his Praetorian Prefect and now Emperor. The Parthian king Artabanus has invaded, furious at Caracalla’s treachery.",
 "debrief": "In Herodian’s and Cassius Dio’s accounts, the battle lasted three days. The Romans scattered caltrops that brought down the Parthian cataphracts and camel riders, but the Parthians overlapped the Roman line. After huge losses, Macrinus made peace by paying Artabanus about 200 million sesterces. His soldiers despised the payment, and he was overthrown within a year. It was the last great battle against Parthia, which soon fell to the Persians. The other choices are what-ifs.",
